  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nMonsoonal moisture flowing north that is interacting with a zonal\njet stream flow has resulted in mainly cloudy skies across\nnortheast Montana this afternoon. The mid-level clouds should\nclear from north to south tonight allowing temps to drop into the\n50s north to the 60s south by Wednesday morning.\n\nSunshine should allow temperatures to begin warming Wednesday,\ntopping out in the 80s across the CWA. Monsoonal moisture\nstreaming north should halt near southern Montana but clouds will\nincrease across the CWA Wednesday night. Showers should stay south\nof the CWA.\n\nAn upper ridge over the western states will build into Montana\nthis week with temps warming into Friday. Look for highs Friday to\nreach the 90s north to the low 100s south. West winds will also\nincrease as a surface low passes east to the northeast of us. If\nfuels dry out enough, there could be Fire Weather concerns.\n\nSomewhat lighter winds are expected Saturday but slightly lower\nhumidities will keep the Fire Weather concerns alive.\n\nSlightly cooler conditions are expected Sunday but not enough to\nremove the Fire Weather concerns. \n\nLighter winds and higher humidity, especially in the northeast\nzones should continue to hack away at the Fire Weather concerns\nMonday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nGoing NBM forecast looked good today and didn't stray away with\nthis package. Some shower potential Thursday night may allow for\nan oportunity to become more specific as time draws closer. TFJ",
